# Typography type scale (mandatory)

Before adding or changing any text styles, follow `skills/typography.md` and the type scale in `skills/primitives.md` (Typography section).

## Allowed `font-size` values only

`11` · `12` · `14` · `16` · `18` · `20` · `24` · `32` · `40` · `48` · `56` · `72` (px)

| Role | Size / line-height | Notes |
|------|--------------------|--------|
| label-sm / overline | 11 / 14 or 16 | Absolute minimum; badges, eyebrows |
| label-md / caption | 12 / 16 | Form labels, fine print |
| body-sm / label-lg | 14 / 20 | Body floor; supporting UI |
| body-md | 16 / 24 | Default body |
| body-lg / heading-sm | 18 / 28 or 24 | Lead / small heading |
| heading-md | 20 / 28 | Card / sheet titles |
| heading-lg | 24 / 32 | Section titles |
| heading-xl | 32 / 40 | Large amounts / page emphasis |
| display-* | 40+ | Marketing heroes only |

## Hard rules

- **Never** use off-scale sizes (`10px`, `13px`, `15px`, `17px`, `19px`, `22px`, `28px`, `34px`, etc.).
- If a design/spec uses an off-scale size, **snap to the nearest allowed size** (e.g. `13 → 14`, `10 → 11`, `15 → 14` or `16`).
- Pair size with the matching line-height from the table above (do not leave orphan `18px`/`19px` line-heights on `14px` text).
- Font family: `'Euclid Circular B', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, sans-serif`.
- Body text minimum **14px**; labels minimum **12px**; never below **11px**.
- Prefer semantic tokens / comments naming the variant (`/* body-sm */`) when hardcoding in CSS modules.
- Do not invent one-off sizes for density; use `label-sm` / `caption` instead of shrinking body.

## Examples

```scss
/* ❌ BAD */
font-size: 13px;
line-height: 18px;

/* ✅ GOOD — body-sm */
font-size: 14px;
line-height: 20px;
```

```scss
/* ❌ BAD */
font-size: 10px;

/* ✅ GOOD — label-sm / overline */
font-size: 11px;
line-height: 14px; /* or 16px for overline */
```
